:"2025-05-04T22:37:39Z","updated_at":"2025-05-26T16:30:33Z","closed_at":"2025-05-26T16:30:29Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot v4.5.dev (1cf573f44) - master, since https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105147\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 (build 26100) - Single-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2070 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7602) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-10750H CPU @ 2.60GHz (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nResizing a Sprite with Ctrl held now adjusts the region rect when control is held, instead of just being for smart snapping. They should be two separate actions.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/07536947-e57f-4b8c-9fff-2177c16515d0\n\nThe region rect editing was added by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105147, and it uses the control key.\nHowever the control key is already in use for the smart snapping, so the region rect editing should be accessed in a different way.\nAll modifier keys are already in use, so it can't just be moved to another one.\n\nTo fix this, I think the Sprite Editor Plugin should have it as a separate tool mode, like how the Path2D Editor Plugin has its own tool modes.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Add a sprite.\n- Enable the region rect.\n- Hold control and drag the rect side to resize; try use to smart snap.\n- It will adjust the region rect and smart snap at the same time.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https